 "drivingQuestion": "What is shemen hamor?",
 "outcome": "inconclusive",
 "outcomeNote": "two glosses of shemen hamor; a baraita appears to support the second without the Gemara deciding",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "pesachim.43a.1",
   "daf": "43a",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "שֶׁהִגִּיעוּ לְפִרְקָן, וְלֹא הִגִּיעוּ לְשָׁנִים, בְּנוֹת עֲנִיִּים — טוֹפְלוֹת אוֹתָן בְּסִיד, בְּנוֹת עֲשִׁירִים — טוֹפְלוֹת אוֹתָן בְּסוֹלֶת, בְּנוֹת מְלָכִים — בְּשֶׁמֶן הַמּוֹר, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״שִׁשָּׁה חֳדָשִׁים בְּשֶׁמֶן הַמּוֹר״.",
   "en": "«who reached» physical «maturity, but had not» yet «reached the age» of majority, and women who sought to remove hair for cosmetic purposes: «They would smear daughters of the poor with lime; they would smear daughters of the wealthy with fine flour; they would smear daughters of kings with shemen hamor, as it was stated:» “For so were the days of their anointing filled, «six months with shemen hamor”» (Esther 2:12)."
  },
  {
   "id": "pesachim.43a.2",
   "daf": "43a",
   "sentenceId": 1,
   "he": "מַאי ״שֶׁמֶן הַמּוֹר״? רַב הוּנָא בַּר יִרְמְיָה אוֹמֵר: סְטָכַת. רַב יִרְמְיָה בַּר אַבָּא אָמַר: שֶׁמֶן זַיִת שֶׁלֹּא הֵבִיא שְׁלִישׁ.",
   "en": "The Gemara asks: «What is shemen hamor? Rav Huna bar Ḥiyya said: Setaket. Rav Yirmeya bar Abba said:» It is «olive oil» extracted from an olive «that» has «not» yet «reached a third» of its growth; the acidic oil is effective as a depilatory."
  },
  {
   "id": "pesachim.43a.3",
   "daf": "43a",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "תַּנְיָא רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר: אַנְפִּיקְנִין — שֶׁמֶן זַיִת שֶׁלֹּא הֵבִיא שְׁלִישׁ, וְלָמָּה סָכִין אוֹתוֹ? מִפְּנֵי שֶׁמַּשִּׁיר אֶת הַשֵּׂיעָר וּמְעַדֵּן אֶת הַבָּשָׂר.",
   "en": "«It was taught» in a baraita: «Rabbi Yehuda says» that «anpiknin» is «olive oil» from an olive «that has not reached a third» of its growth. «And why is it spread» on the body? It is «due to» the fact «that it removes [mashir] the hair and pampers the skin.»"
  }
 ],
